# rule.always.itemize-the-fulcrums-you-best-guess

when you best-guess a fork mid-drive, itemize it **at that moment**; never at the end, never only in yield prose.

```
$route/.fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums._.md               # SUMMARY
$route/.fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F$n-$slug.md  # one ENTRY per fulcrum
```

both owed. append at the moment, never in a sweep. a call under 93% confidence is a trigger too, even with no fork (n=1 generalization, unfetched premise, invented taxonomy, an act against a stated bound).

each entry opens with yaml frontmatter: `case · rework · ground · confidence · status · owed · holds · lean · verdict` (a refusal prints the block). body: the fork stated fairly · taken, why · rework, why · confidence, why low · where.

blocker: a fulcrum never itemized · row with no entry or entry with no row · record swept at the end · absent `rework` · prose filename · invalid frontmatter · unrecorded verdict · sub-93% call with no row · percentage with no reason.
